From 2c697eb107e9d447a23279294e975557754688e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew <matthewhale@live.com.au>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:12:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 02/59] XvT targeting computer, XvT laser/ion sounds, Z target
 view

- render.xvt_targeting_computer: the CMD (and a floating copy with the
  cockpit off) shows XvT's layout: target name, SHD/HULL/SYS, a live 3D
  model of the target seen along the pilot's line of sight, orders (word
  wrapped), cargo or order target, and range. X-Wing's own CMD panes and
  lock cross are hidden while it is on. 1998 flight only.
- audio.xvt_weapon_sounds: the six cannon bolt sounds come from XvT's WAVs
  (resources/xvt_weapon_sounds, copied at packaging), converted to VOC;
  charged fighter shots use the fighter sound, not the turbolaser one.
- view_target (Z): chase camera on the current target; Z again returns,
  and the view ends when the target explodes.
